WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.168 --> 00:00:01.690
(upbeat music)

00:00:01.690 --> 00:00:04.420
- The legend around this
chalk is that it's impossible

00:00:04.420 --> 00:00:06.390
to write a false theorem.

00:00:06.390 --> 00:00:09.288
- I assume the special
ingredient was angel tears.

00:00:09.288 --> 00:00:12.370
- Mathematicians from all
of the top schools very

00:00:12.370 --> 00:00:13.847
frequently use it.

00:00:13.847 --> 00:00:16.408
- It's a cult favorite.

00:00:16.408 --> 00:00:18.498
- As soon as I use it I was a convert.

00:00:18.498 --> 00:00:22.200
- The chalk is one of
the best kept secrets in

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:23.560
the math world.

00:00:23.560 --> 00:00:25.202
- It's the Rolls Royce of chalk.

00:00:25.202 --> 00:00:27.785
(gentle music)

00:00:29.380 --> 00:00:31.800
(chalk scratching)

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:34.420
- Hagoromo is a brand of Japanese chalk.

00:00:34.420 --> 00:00:37.130
The way it flows on a board
is a bit hard to describe

00:00:37.130 --> 00:00:38.242
in words.

00:00:38.242 --> 00:00:39.970
- It's really hard to get.

00:00:39.970 --> 00:00:41.620
You can only get it from
Japan, you need a Japanese

00:00:41.620 --> 00:00:43.600
person to bring it back for you.

00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:45.900
- I discovered it when I went to visit the

00:00:45.900 --> 00:00:48.461
University of Tokyo and
one of the professors there

00:00:48.461 --> 00:00:50.482
said to me, you know, we have better chalk

00:00:50.482 --> 00:00:53.210
than you do in the States
and I said, oh go on,

00:00:53.210 --> 00:00:54.400
chalk is chalk.

00:00:54.400 --> 00:00:57.821
And so I tried it out, and
I was surprised to find

00:00:57.821 --> 00:00:58.860
that he was right.

00:00:58.860 --> 00:01:02.540
- I tried it, and I
thought it was phenomenal.

00:01:02.540 --> 00:01:04.650
It's the densest, it erases the cleanest,

00:01:04.650 --> 00:01:06.670
it leaves the nicest line.

00:01:06.670 --> 00:01:08.380
- If you use bad chalk
often you have to press

00:01:08.380 --> 00:01:10.320
really hard for anyone to
see what you're writing

00:01:10.320 --> 00:01:12.750
so using Hagoromo on a good
board, it doesn't really

00:01:12.750 --> 00:01:14.920
feel like you're working hard to write.

00:01:14.920 --> 00:01:17.640
- When I'm teaching I
get a feeling of energy,

00:01:17.640 --> 00:01:20.920
confidence, and the
chalk absolutely helps.

00:01:20.920 --> 00:01:23.270
(chalk clacking)

00:01:23.270 --> 00:01:26.597
- Slowly the math world
has become aware of this,

00:01:26.597 --> 00:01:30.882
and it became a bit of
a fad in some circles.

00:01:30.882 --> 00:01:33.430
(upbeat music)

00:01:33.430 --> 00:01:36.450
- It was like maybe four
years ago the word came out

00:01:36.450 --> 00:01:38.260
that the company was
going out of business.

00:01:38.260 --> 00:01:40.937
I sort of jokingly referred
to it as a chalk apocalypse.

00:01:40.937 --> 00:01:43.602
So I immediately started
hoarding up as much as I could.

00:01:43.602 --> 00:01:46.640
- I ordered three boxes
of Hagoromo and kept it in

00:01:46.640 --> 00:01:49.090
my office and used it very sparingly.

00:01:49.090 --> 00:01:51.340
- I should've bought more but
I have friends that bought

00:01:51.340 --> 00:01:53.800
boxes and boxes and boxes of the stuff.

00:01:53.800 --> 00:01:56.482
They might very well be set
for the rest of their career.

00:01:56.482 --> 00:01:59.090
- We've got like 1,500 sticks.

00:01:59.090 --> 00:02:01.500
That's a lot of days, four sticks a day.

00:02:01.500 --> 00:02:02.660
I think I'm gonna make it.

00:02:02.660 --> 00:02:05.320
- I have probably a 10-year
supply still at home.

00:02:05.320 --> 00:02:07.770
- I calculated how many boxes
would I need to last for

00:02:07.770 --> 00:02:09.442
10 or 15 years.

00:02:09.442 --> 00:02:12.710
I didn't wanna become a chalk
dealer, but I did like the

00:02:12.710 --> 00:02:15.820
idea that I could be
the first stick is free

00:02:15.820 --> 00:02:17.698
chalk dealer on the
block in my department.

00:02:17.698 --> 00:02:20.570
- I was probably selling
it regularly to maybe

00:02:20.570 --> 00:02:21.930
eight to 10 colleagues.

00:02:21.930 --> 00:02:23.770
I would reach into my
cupboard in my office

00:02:23.770 --> 00:02:26.210
and pull out another
box and we'd do the deal

00:02:26.210 --> 00:02:27.043
in my office.

00:02:27.043 --> 00:02:28.680
Yeah, we all had a chalk fix.

00:02:28.680 --> 00:02:30.061
And we still do.

00:02:30.061 --> 00:02:32.644
(gentle music)

00:02:34.717 --> 00:02:38.098
- The original Hagoromo
chalk is slowly disappearing.

00:02:38.098 --> 00:02:42.301
A few years ago, a Korean
company bought their formulas

00:02:42.301 --> 00:02:44.920
and did the best job of
faithfully reproducing it

00:02:44.920 --> 00:02:46.018
in Korea.

00:02:46.018 --> 00:02:48.521
- It was mixed emotions.

00:02:48.521 --> 00:02:50.960
I was happy to know that
it would still be made.

00:02:50.960 --> 00:02:53.060
But I was a little disappointed
that I was less clever

00:02:53.060 --> 00:02:54.461
than I thought I was.

00:02:54.461 --> 00:02:56.340
(gentle music)

00:02:56.340 --> 00:02:59.830
- In many ways mathematics
is like craftsmanship,

00:02:59.830 --> 00:03:01.490
in some ways it's like artistry;

00:03:01.490 --> 00:03:03.380
in some ways it's like science.

00:03:03.380 --> 00:03:05.630
But there's a real high
craft side to getting

00:03:05.630 --> 00:03:07.842
a beautiful lecture on a blackboard.

00:03:07.842 --> 00:03:10.820
Mathematicians admire this in each other

00:03:10.820 --> 00:03:14.100
and like to use the best tools for it.

00:03:14.100 --> 00:03:16.560
- There's incredible value
to this but the value

00:03:16.560 --> 00:03:19.842
is in using it up, not hoarding it.

00:03:19.842 --> 00:03:22.425
(gentle music)

